From 5e5f6538b3611da58998319d5d0231e6250bb47b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dxbjavid <dxbjavid@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 15:56:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] dns: reject rdata larger than the 16 bit rdlength field

avahi_rdata_parse() takes the rdata size as a size_t but passes it
straight into parse_rdata(), whose rdlength parameter is a uint16_t, so
any size of 65536 bytes or more is silently truncated mod 65536. A
65536 byte buffer for instance is parsed as a zero length record while
avahi_rdata_parse() still returns success, so the record that ends up
published has nothing to do with what the caller passed in.

This is not a crash and it is only reachable from a local client through
EntryGroup.AddRecord, which hands its byte array to avahi_rdata_parse()
unchecked. Reject sizes above AVAHI_DNS_RDATA_MAX before the narrowing,
matching the assert already present in avahi_rdata_serialize().

Caught by the implicit-conversion UBSan check:

  dns.c:869:35: runtime error: implicit conversion from type 'size_t'
  (aka 'unsigned long') of value 65536 (64-bit, unsigned) to type
  'uint16_t' (aka 'unsigned short') changed the value to 0 (16-bit,
  unsigned)
      #0 avahi_rdata_parse dns.c:869
      #1 main dns-test.c:181

The regression test that triggers it is added in the following commit.
---
 avahi-core/dns.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/avahi-core/dns.c b/avahi-core/dns.c
index 3ac9621..b433795 100644
--- a/avahi-core/dns.c
+++ b/avahi-core/dns.c
@@ -860,6 +860,12 @@ int avahi_rdata_parse(AvahiRecord *record, const void* rdata, size_t size) {
     assert(record);
     assert(rdata);
 
+    /* rdlength is a 16 bit field on the wire and parse_rdata() takes it
+     * as a uint16_t, so anything bigger would be silently truncated and
+     * parsed as an unrelated length. Reject it instead. */
+    if (size > AVAHI_DNS_RDATA_MAX)
+        return -1;
+
     p.data = (void*) rdata;
     p.max_size = p.size = size;
     p.rindex = 0;
